1
00:00:41,959 --> 00:00:47,965
THE PERFECT LIE

2
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:54,638
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

3
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,975
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS
AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

4
00:01:19,037 --> 00:01:20,205
[Jisun] Did you get it?

5
00:01:28,297 --> 00:01:29,756
What are you going to do with it?

6
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:37,389
[Jisun] I'm going to make him understand
what he's done.

7
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:43,770
MIN JUNHO

8
00:01:43,854 --> 00:01:44,896
[Jisun] <i>Let's meet.</i>

9
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:47,733
<i>I want to start my life over.</i>

10
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,943
<i>I'll do whatever you say.</i>

11
00:02:18,639 --> 00:02:20,015
-What the…
-Oh, my gosh.

12
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:34,112
Where are you going? We need to talk.

13
00:02:34,196 --> 00:02:35,197
[Junho] You're drunk.

14
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:49,252
What the…

15
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:56,009
You…

16
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:04,434
Goddamn it!

17
00:03:16,488 --> 00:03:17,739
Just close your eyes.

18
00:03:20,701 --> 00:03:22,160
-[gearshift clicks]
-[exhales sharply]

19
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:30,293
EPISODE 6
THE VICTIMS

20
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,666
What the hell are you doing?

21
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:53,418
What?

22
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:56,129
You don't like it
now that the tables have turned?

23
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:03,929
That'll last a few hours.
That's how it works.

24
00:05:10,936 --> 00:05:12,646
You're really doing this?

25
00:05:14,064 --> 00:05:15,065
To me?

26
00:05:16,233 --> 00:05:18,068
What makes you think I can't?

27
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:33,583
You have no idea how many times
I've imagined this moment.

28
00:05:50,225 --> 00:05:51,601
Having fun?

29
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,272
Turning into a perpetrator for a change?

30
00:05:57,107 --> 00:05:58,483
I thought it'd be fun.

31
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:01,486
But I just feel even more disgusted.

32
00:06:02,654 --> 00:06:04,406
Don't you still have a lot of questions?

33
00:06:07,367 --> 00:06:09,619
You haven't heard anything
directly from me yet.

34
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:18,336
[Jisun] That night…

35
00:06:19,296 --> 00:06:20,714
You chose a day with heavy rain,

36
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:23,008
so you'd have an excuse
to come in, didn't you?

37
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,223
You're out of your mind.

38
00:06:31,182 --> 00:06:33,643
Yeah, laugh while you still can.

39
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:38,732
I guess that's just human nature.

40
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:41,276
You never really understand
what someone's going through

41
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:43,111
until you experience it yourself.

42
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:50,535
I searched online

43
00:06:51,328 --> 00:06:54,706
for ways to deal with you
and what kind of punishment you deserve.

44
00:06:55,749 --> 00:06:57,751
I thought I'd tap into
the collective wisdom.

45
00:07:00,170 --> 00:07:03,131
Turns out there are so many people
who've been through what I have.

46
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:05,884
People who couldn't report it,

47
00:07:05,967 --> 00:07:07,844
or who did but ended up hurt
all over again

48
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:09,721
because the punishment was so lenient.

49
00:07:11,348 --> 00:07:12,557
Minors.

50
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:16,227
A lot of men too.

51
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:20,440
They say it's crucial to help.

52
00:07:21,775 --> 00:07:23,818
That if they can't
bring themselves to do it…

53
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:28,782
-you have to get rid of…
-[box cutter clicks]

54
00:07:29,908 --> 00:07:31,368
…the root of the problem for them.

55
00:07:40,043 --> 00:07:41,670
You remember what you did, don't you?

56
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:42,921
DEAR MY FRIEND IS NOW OPEN

57
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:46,257
One person is dead, and the other
can't live a normal life anymore.

58
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:51,054
Ms. Kim Jeongmi couldn't even report
what you did to her.

59
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:55,433
She blames herself for her friend's death
and lives like she's the guilty one.

60
00:08:07,404 --> 00:08:09,155
LOCATION DETAILS

61
00:08:30,385 --> 00:08:32,595
CAPTAIN

62
00:08:35,515 --> 00:08:37,350
-[team leader] <i>Hello?</i>
-Hello, sir.

63
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:40,145
It's nothing urgent.

64
00:08:40,228 --> 00:08:41,938
I just wanted to keep you in the loop.

65
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:45,942
<i>It's just that</i>
<i>Min Junho's location is a bit…</i>

66
00:08:46,026 --> 00:08:47,235
[team leader] <i>What about his location?</i>

67
00:08:49,779 --> 00:08:51,573
I'm just getting a bad feeling.

68
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,044
INCOMING CALL
MY HUSBAND

69
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:08,465
Yeah, I'm on my way home.

70
00:09:09,591 --> 00:09:12,010
I'll be home soon,
so I'll make sure to get some rest.

71
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:17,015
Okay. You too, honey.

72
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:30,195
How did Ms. Joo Eunhye die?

73
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:37,077
I had a patient
who took their own life with drugs.

74
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:42,749
I told Eunhye
exactly how that patient did it.

75
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:49,964
So she wouldn't fail.

76
00:09:51,216 --> 00:09:54,010
I didn't think she'd actually
go through with it, to be honest.

77
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:59,057
I was a little surprised
when she pulled it off.

78
00:10:01,351 --> 00:10:02,727
Why?

79
00:10:02,811 --> 00:10:04,521
Why would you do that to your own wife?

80
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:08,775
Because that's what she wanted.

81
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:11,111
What?

82
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:14,989
[Junho] When I told her what I'd done…

83
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:19,452
with her friend…

84
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:26,251
-The look on her face--
-You drove her to take her own life.

85
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:27,710
No.

86
00:10:27,794 --> 00:10:32,215
That was the bravest thing
Eunhye did in her life.

87
00:10:34,092 --> 00:10:38,388
And I was the only one who understood
and respected her decision.

88
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:41,891
You deliberately used GHB
to make Kim Jeongmi your victim,

89
00:10:42,475 --> 00:10:47,522
just to push Eunhye
into ending her life sooner.

90
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:52,318
What are you talking about?

91
00:10:52,861 --> 00:10:55,071
-I'm not that kind of person.
-Liar.

92
00:10:58,324 --> 00:11:00,076
Isn't this what you wanted to hear?

93
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:04,622
-You're recording all this, right?
-[scoffs] You piece of trash.

94
00:11:05,165 --> 00:11:09,711
Kang Jisun, how about you act
a little more mature, huh?

95
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:14,799
I'm not going to make
the same mistake this time.

96
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,051
"This time"?

97
00:11:17,135 --> 00:11:19,554
At first, I thought it would be simple.

98
00:11:22,307 --> 00:11:25,018
I thought all I had to do
was tell the truth, but I was wrong.

99
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:28,229
So this time,
I'm going to be the one lying.

100
00:11:28,313 --> 00:11:31,149
I'll say you brought me here.

101
00:11:33,318 --> 00:11:36,446
-Who's going to believe that?
-Plenty of people saw us at the bar.

102
00:11:36,529 --> 00:11:38,698
Min Junho!

103
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:43,786
I'll call the police early in the morning
and show them the rope marks on my wrists.

104
00:11:43,870 --> 00:11:45,580
I don't even know where we are.

105
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:47,582
They'll find GHB in your car too.

106
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:51,252
I'll say you got that wound on your neck
when I tried to escape,

107
00:11:51,336 --> 00:11:55,298
and that I somehow managed
to knock you down and tie you up.

108
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:01,471
So now, you're going to take one hard hit.

109
00:12:03,014 --> 00:12:04,432
-Would that make you feel better?

110
00:12:04,515 --> 00:12:06,559
Not nearly enough
to make up for what you did.

111
00:12:06,643 --> 00:12:09,187
You sold your dignity
for a mere five million won,

112
00:12:09,771 --> 00:12:13,316
in exchange for putting up with
Principal Jeong's sexual harassment.

113
00:12:15,026 --> 00:12:18,029
-I wasn't the one who took the money.
-But you didn't give it back.

114
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:22,033
You put a price on the pain
and suffering you endured.

115
00:12:23,493 --> 00:12:24,827
In the end…

116
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:29,123
you sold your self-respect
for five million won.

117
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:31,125
Don't be ridiculous!

118
00:12:40,343 --> 00:12:41,511
[Junho] Unfortunately for you,

119
00:12:42,553 --> 00:12:44,764
I think we both know
how this is going to end.

120
00:12:56,651 --> 00:12:58,027
You're not getting away.

121
00:13:14,502 --> 00:13:15,712
Damn it.

122
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:29,475
Damn it.

123
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:51,265
Ms. Kang!

124
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:55,478
Help me! He tried to kill me!

125
00:14:57,897 --> 00:14:58,981
Help me.

126
00:14:59,065 --> 00:15:00,650
She's lying, Detective.

127
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:03,111
She drugged me
and dragged me all the way here

128
00:15:03,194 --> 00:15:05,279
to make it look like
I planned the whole thing.

129
00:15:23,673 --> 00:15:28,219
How am I supposed to believe a man
who drugs and sexually assaults women?

130
00:15:40,398 --> 00:15:42,525
Do you have any evidence, Detective?

131
00:15:42,608 --> 00:15:44,443
You saw him attack me, didn't you?

132
00:15:44,527 --> 00:15:46,904
-Arrest him, now!
-She's the one who held me captive

133
00:15:46,988 --> 00:15:49,282
and attacked me first.
I was acting in self-defense.

134
00:15:49,907 --> 00:15:51,075
If you don't believe me…

135
00:15:52,827 --> 00:15:54,287
go ahead and arrest me right now.

136
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,589
[Jisun] What are you doing?

137
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:07,592
-You're just letting him go?
-If we arrest him now

138
00:16:07,675 --> 00:16:09,510
and a drug test comes back positive,

139
00:16:10,428 --> 00:16:11,929
you'll be the one in trouble.

140
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,317
I swear I'll catch you!

141
00:16:25,484 --> 00:16:28,070
I'll find proof that you
sexually assaulted me!

142
00:16:28,154 --> 00:16:29,739
I swear I will!

143
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:42,710
I didn't do anything wrong.

144
00:16:44,921 --> 00:16:47,131
I think you've got it all wrong.

145
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:22,667
[Jisun] Back then, I…

146
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:32,343
I guess I cursed you when I said
you'd understand if it happened to you.

147
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:36,973
Ms. Kang.

148
00:17:39,642 --> 00:17:42,603
Thanks to your call that morning,

149
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:45,982
I got the drug test.

150
00:17:48,818 --> 00:17:50,611
If it hadn't been for you,

151
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:54,740
I never would've known
something like that had happened to me…

152
00:17:55,950 --> 00:17:58,619
or that Min Junho was the one who did it.

153
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:11,257
I'm sorry…

154
00:18:15,636 --> 00:18:17,346
for making you fight this battle alone.

155
00:18:20,558 --> 00:18:22,435
But now, when it comes to Min Junho…

156
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:25,771
you're not alone anymore.

157
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:38,159
Are you going to be okay?

158
00:19:33,381 --> 00:19:34,382
[Hyunsoo] Dad?

159
00:19:36,342 --> 00:19:37,343
Hey.

160
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:40,096
Did I wake you?

161
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:41,514
Why are you home so late?

162
00:19:42,807 --> 00:19:45,935
Well, things just keep coming up lately.

163
00:19:55,778 --> 00:19:56,779
Hyunsoo.

164
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:02,827
It looks like I'm going to…

165
00:20:03,994 --> 00:20:06,038
get questioned by the police again.

166
00:20:06,789 --> 00:20:08,165
Why?

167
00:20:08,791 --> 00:20:11,502
They're saying I committed another crime.

168
00:20:12,545 --> 00:20:14,088
But that's ridiculous.

169
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:16,132
Why do they keep doing this?

170
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:18,759
I guess they're desperate
to make me out to be a criminal,

171
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:22,138
even if they have to frame me.

172
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:24,390
Then you just have to prove
you didn't do it.

173
00:20:33,441 --> 00:20:34,525
That day…

174
00:20:35,985 --> 00:20:38,487
I went for a walk by myself.

175
00:20:39,739 --> 00:20:41,866
<i>The day the police are talking about.</i>

176
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:45,661
<i>You were home, Hyunsoo.</i>

177
00:20:47,997 --> 00:20:49,081
<i>So…</i>

178
00:20:51,292 --> 00:20:54,086
it's hard for me to prove
I didn't do anything wrong.

179
00:20:56,088 --> 00:20:57,798
But you didn't do anything wrong.

180
00:21:00,634 --> 00:21:05,598
These people wouldn't think twice
about putting me in prison.

181
00:21:10,644 --> 00:21:12,271
If I get arrested…

182
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:16,233
everything I've worked so hard for…

183
00:21:21,322 --> 00:21:22,907
Even you, Hyunsoo…

184
00:21:26,327 --> 00:21:28,579
The thought of losing it all
is tearing me apart.

185
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:35,503
What if I tell them
I was with you that day, Dad?

186
00:21:36,754 --> 00:21:37,755
You can't.

187
00:21:37,838 --> 00:21:40,382
You lied to help Soyeon back then too.

188
00:21:42,510 --> 00:21:44,428
You said it was a white lie.

189
00:21:46,639 --> 00:21:48,182
I want to help you too.

190
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:02,613
You said family is supposed
to protect each other.

191
00:22:05,533 --> 00:22:07,660
I can't make you lie too.

192
00:22:08,285 --> 00:22:09,328
I'm going to do it.

193
00:22:10,663 --> 00:22:12,998
I won't let them take you away.

194
00:22:17,169 --> 00:22:18,587
I love you, my son.

195
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:35,646
Sir?

196
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:39,275
Sir.

197
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:40,484
Oh, hey.

198
00:22:41,151 --> 00:22:42,444
You're here early.

199
00:22:43,153 --> 00:22:44,446
Can we talk for a minute?

200
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:50,202
So, because there's no evidence…

201
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:55,708
you're telling me to keep my mouth shut,
take some time off, and stay out of it?

202
00:22:55,791 --> 00:22:58,210
I'm saying we need to
think this through carefully.

203
00:22:58,294 --> 00:22:59,420
This isn't just…

204
00:23:00,671 --> 00:23:02,006
a personal matter.

205
00:23:03,507 --> 00:23:07,761
Look, it's a sensitive time
with performance reviews coming up.

206
00:23:08,679 --> 00:23:11,849
People are already saying
there's been a lack of discipline.

207
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:15,102
If this goes south, it'll take everyone
from the top down with it.

208
00:23:15,686 --> 00:23:18,230
So the higher-ups think
delaying or covering it up

209
00:23:18,314 --> 00:23:20,232
will help their chances
of getting promoted.

210
00:23:20,316 --> 00:23:22,067
Oh, come on.

211
00:23:22,151 --> 00:23:24,403
They were furious
when they heard about this.

212
00:23:26,488 --> 00:23:28,574
What does he take the police for?

213
00:23:29,074 --> 00:23:32,286
They're determined to get that bastard
when the time comes.

214
00:23:32,369 --> 00:23:34,204
But what if something goes wrong

215
00:23:35,039 --> 00:23:39,001
and those vultures in the press
get wind of it?

216
00:23:39,585 --> 00:23:41,128
They'll say a female police officer

217
00:23:41,211 --> 00:23:43,797
couldn't even protect herself,
let alone catch the suspect.

218
00:23:43,881 --> 00:23:45,925
They'll question whether
she's even fit to be--

219
00:23:46,008 --> 00:23:47,176
Sir!

220
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:51,805
I'm saying some lunatic
might go around talking like that.

221
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:57,478
You're about to become a mother.

222
00:23:58,938 --> 00:24:01,690
The higher-ups are trying to protect you.

223
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:06,111
I'll keep it quiet.

224
00:24:07,071 --> 00:24:08,781
And you never told me to take time off.

225
00:24:12,242 --> 00:24:14,203
-This case…

226
00:24:14,286 --> 00:24:16,121
We're not covering it up.

227
00:24:16,205 --> 00:24:17,706
I promise. Trust me, okay?

228
00:24:19,959 --> 00:24:21,502
Even when I'm trying to sleep,

229
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:23,629
the thought of that bastard just…

230
00:24:25,172 --> 00:24:27,466
I have a daughter of my own too, you know.

231
00:24:29,718 --> 00:24:33,180
Wait. Nothing happened last night, right?

232
00:24:37,059 --> 00:24:38,310
No.

233
00:24:38,394 --> 00:24:39,436
Nothing happened.

234
00:24:40,771 --> 00:24:45,109
Just focus on taking care of yourself
until the baby's born, got it?

235
00:26:21,163 --> 00:26:22,664
ANTI-ANXIETY MEDICATION

236
00:26:49,233 --> 00:26:51,485
Min Junho isn't going to just let this go.

237
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:54,446
He'll find some way to get back at me.

238
00:26:54,530 --> 00:26:57,658
It's natural to feel unsafe
when the crime happened in your own home

239
00:26:57,741 --> 00:26:59,368
or the perpetrator lives nearby.

240
00:26:59,451 --> 00:27:01,328
<i>And it can actually be dangerous too.</i>

241
00:27:02,496 --> 00:27:05,666
So you're telling me to move or something?

242
00:27:06,708 --> 00:27:08,627
Of course, it's up to you.

243
00:27:09,128 --> 00:27:11,547
<i>It's not running away.</i>
<i>It's about protecting yourself.</i>

244
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:13,340
<i>You can't afford to lose your strength.</i>

245
00:27:20,013 --> 00:27:21,348
What about you?

246
00:27:21,932 --> 00:27:23,767
I'm a police officer, you know.

247
00:27:25,519 --> 00:27:26,770
For now,

248
00:27:26,854 --> 00:27:29,648
just focus on protecting yourself
and regain some peace of mind.

249
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:32,234
We're going to get Min Junho.

250
00:27:33,485 --> 00:27:36,196
Because he won't be able
to stop himself from doing it again.

251
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:54,756
CCTV RECORDING IN PROGRESS
CONTINUOUS RECORDING

252
00:27:55,591 --> 00:27:58,302
[attorney] We're more than happy
to cooperate with the police,

253
00:27:59,136 --> 00:28:02,347
but questioning him as a witness
without even telling us what it's about…

254
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:05,434
I'm not too thrilled about that.

255
00:28:06,602 --> 00:28:09,855
We're just trying to rule out
the possibility of false testimony.

256
00:28:10,689 --> 00:28:15,485
As you know, he's a minor
who could be influenced by his guardian.

257
00:28:17,571 --> 00:28:19,656
So you're saying
his guardian can't be trusted?

258
00:28:24,453 --> 00:28:26,121
Just tell me what you remember.

259
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:28,081
Only the truth.

260
00:28:31,043 --> 00:28:34,338
Do you remember the day your mom died?

261
00:28:34,421 --> 00:28:35,672
[attorney] Hold on a second.

262
00:28:37,925 --> 00:28:40,594
Is that question actually relevant
to your investigation?

263
00:28:40,677 --> 00:28:43,847
It may or may not be,
depending on his answer.

264
00:28:46,892 --> 00:28:48,727
He's a child who needs to be protected.

265
00:28:48,810 --> 00:28:50,354
That's a sensitive personal matter.

266
00:28:51,104 --> 00:28:54,483
If necessary, we can reschedule
with a child psychologist present.

267
00:28:58,445 --> 00:28:59,863
Let me ask you again.

268
00:29:01,949 --> 00:29:06,662
Can you tell me what you did
after school last Thursday?

269
00:29:10,582 --> 00:29:12,042
I went straight home.

270
00:29:15,128 --> 00:29:17,047
I borrowed a book
from the library that day…

271
00:29:20,133 --> 00:29:21,176
so I read it…

272
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:25,597
and had dinner with my dad.

273
00:29:28,058 --> 00:29:29,726
Do you remember the title of the book?

274
00:29:34,147 --> 00:29:35,691
<i>Fabre's Book of Insects</i>.

275
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:41,363
-[chuckles]
-[scribbling]

276
00:29:43,031 --> 00:29:45,826
But doesn't your dad scold you
if you play video games?

277
00:29:45,909 --> 00:29:48,120
I played with my headset on
so he wouldn't know.

278
00:29:48,203 --> 00:29:49,204
[Hwayoung] Hmm.

279
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:52,082
What was your dad doing at the time?

280
00:30:03,010 --> 00:30:04,636
He was in his room.

281
00:30:06,179 --> 00:30:07,973
He didn't leave the house?

282
00:30:08,056 --> 00:30:09,808
Not even for a little while?

283
00:30:11,476 --> 00:30:12,477
No.

284
00:30:13,687 --> 00:30:15,856
Maybe you were too busy gaming to notice?

285
00:30:18,859 --> 00:30:19,943
Let me ask you again.

286
00:30:21,236 --> 00:30:23,697
How do you know your dad didn't go out?

287
00:30:24,531 --> 00:30:27,325
-I didn't hear him leave.
-But you said you had your headset on.

288
00:30:29,453 --> 00:30:30,746
You don't have to answer.

289
00:30:32,456 --> 00:30:34,708
Those are leading questions,
don't you think?

290
00:30:38,170 --> 00:30:39,755
After I was done playing…

291
00:30:44,134 --> 00:30:45,594
at around 10:00 p.m…

292
00:30:47,054 --> 00:30:49,056
I got thirsty,
so I stepped out for a minute.

293
00:30:52,851 --> 00:30:57,105
Dad was closing the curtains,
and he asked if I'd brushed my teeth.

294
00:31:01,777 --> 00:31:02,778
I see.

295
00:31:03,987 --> 00:31:04,988
All right.

296
00:31:06,990 --> 00:31:09,326
Do you remember
the last time you saw your mom?

297
00:31:09,409 --> 00:31:10,535
[attorney] What are you doing?

298
00:31:10,619 --> 00:31:11,870
[Hwayoung] Hyunsoo has a good memory,

299
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:14,664
so I figured he'd remember
what happened three years ago.

300
00:31:14,748 --> 00:31:16,041
It wasn't in the records.

301
00:31:16,124 --> 00:31:18,168
I thought we wouldn't be
asking irrelevant--

302
00:31:18,251 --> 00:31:20,420
I decide what's relevant to the case.

303
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:29,721
The day your mom died,

304
00:31:29,805 --> 00:31:31,056
was anyone at home?

305
00:31:35,685 --> 00:31:36,812
No.

306
00:31:37,729 --> 00:31:39,564
-I was out.
-What about your dad?

307
00:31:39,648 --> 00:31:42,484
-Detective.
-Hyunsoo, just tell me what you saw.

308
00:31:42,567 --> 00:31:44,111
-[attorney] Don't answer.
-Answer me, Hyunsoo.

309
00:31:44,194 --> 00:31:45,195
[team leader] Inspector Lee!

310
00:31:47,239 --> 00:31:49,741
That's enough. Thanks for coming in.
You can go now.

311
00:31:49,825 --> 00:31:50,992
Hyunsoo, let's go. Get up.

312
00:32:00,752 --> 00:32:02,796
What are you doing?
You didn't report this.

313
00:32:02,879 --> 00:32:05,549
I was just questioning a witness,
following proper procedure.

314
00:32:18,645 --> 00:32:20,480
-Is Mom sleeping?
-[door closes]

315
00:32:21,106 --> 00:32:23,108
Mom's not feeling well right now.

316
00:32:24,192 --> 00:32:26,069
Why don't you go play at the playground?

317
00:32:27,028 --> 00:32:28,029
Can I ride my bike?

318
00:32:29,364 --> 00:32:30,365
Sure.

319
00:32:34,244 --> 00:32:35,245
But…

320
00:32:36,913 --> 00:32:39,666
I promised Mom I'd show her this.

321
00:32:42,085 --> 00:32:43,378
I'll show it to her for you.

322
00:33:38,475 --> 00:33:39,559
Your phone.

323
00:33:41,978 --> 00:33:43,355
Where's yours?

324
00:33:43,438 --> 00:33:45,899
I already told you.
My account got suspended.

325
00:33:59,246 --> 00:34:00,372
It sold!

326
00:34:01,665 --> 00:34:03,541
Did you sell another pair of knockoffs?

327
00:34:03,625 --> 00:34:04,876
Yeah.

328
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:07,587
-What if you get caught again?
-I won't.

329
00:34:09,464 --> 00:34:11,424
The buyer specifically asked
for knockoffs.

330
00:34:12,092 --> 00:34:13,802
Isn't that illegal too?

331
00:34:13,885 --> 00:34:16,888
Oh, please. By that logic,
every adult would be a criminal.

332
00:34:17,722 --> 00:34:19,516
Is this how you're going
to live your life?

333
00:34:19,599 --> 00:34:23,019
No, I'm going to be a famous K-pop idol.

334
00:34:23,103 --> 00:34:25,230
What if you end up in jail
before you become one?

335
00:34:39,744 --> 00:34:41,955
Why is that any of your business?

336
00:34:42,038 --> 00:34:45,125
[Junghyeon] Hey,
I'm the one who got you the GHB.

337
00:34:45,208 --> 00:34:48,503
Don't you think you should talk to me
before deciding to give up the fight?

338
00:34:50,130 --> 00:34:54,551
And if you're going to take him on,
you're going to need someone like me.

339
00:34:54,634 --> 00:34:55,760
I appreciate it.

340
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:58,930
But the best way you can help
is to stay out of this.

341
00:35:00,348 --> 00:35:04,227
You still have to see him at the hospital,
so just pretend you don't know anything.

342
00:35:04,311 --> 00:35:06,938
How can I just pretend I don't know
when I'm so furious?

343
00:35:07,439 --> 00:35:10,609
It's bad enough that you lost your job.
Why should you have to move too?

344
00:35:14,029 --> 00:35:15,196
That's enough.

345
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:17,240
If you keep talking,
I'm going to get angry.

346
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:20,076
Okay, okay.

347
00:35:35,717 --> 00:35:37,135
-Huh?
-[clattering]

348
00:35:38,303 --> 00:35:40,639
This looks just like
the one I bought Uyeong.

349
00:35:43,975 --> 00:35:47,145
UYEONG

350
00:35:47,896 --> 00:35:50,315
Is this my sister's?

351
00:35:51,733 --> 00:35:53,652
She must've left it in my car by accident.

352
00:35:54,611 --> 00:35:58,031
She was getting wet in the rain
the other day, so I gave her a ride.

353
00:35:59,199 --> 00:36:01,451
Why was she getting wet
when she had an umbrella?

354
00:36:03,787 --> 00:36:07,082
It's a kids' umbrella, so it's too small.
She was walking all hunched over.

355
00:36:07,791 --> 00:36:10,460
Your sister was worried sick about you
when you disappeared.

356
00:36:12,587 --> 00:36:14,756
[sighs] Look, I'm sure you didn't want to

357
00:36:14,839 --> 00:36:17,133
turn your phone off
and disappear like that.

358
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:19,844
You must've been going through hell.

359
00:36:19,928 --> 00:36:20,929
I get it.

360
00:36:24,641 --> 00:36:27,352
I was just trying to remember
if it rained that day…

361
00:36:29,938 --> 00:36:31,439
but it didn't.

362
00:36:32,774 --> 00:36:34,734
It must've been another day then.

363
00:36:34,818 --> 00:36:36,861
Anyway, we were all really worried.

364
00:36:38,947 --> 00:36:39,948
[Jisun] Okay.

365
00:36:40,907 --> 00:36:42,575
I'll give this back to her.

366
00:36:42,659 --> 00:36:43,702
Sure.

367
00:37:08,226 --> 00:37:09,519
<i>The call cannot be connected…</i>

368
00:37:11,813 --> 00:37:14,816
-[beeping continues]

369
00:37:24,117 --> 00:37:25,326
[spouse] Ta-da!

370
00:37:26,953 --> 00:37:28,747
Wait, hold on.

371
00:37:30,707 --> 00:37:32,625
Park Seokgu, son of the motherland,

372
00:37:32,709 --> 00:37:35,712
reporting for duty to my wife,
Lee Hwayoung!

373
00:37:35,795 --> 00:37:37,756
Ma'am!

374
00:37:41,134 --> 00:37:43,261
What's this? Where's my hug?

375
00:37:43,970 --> 00:37:45,346
Come on!

376
00:37:48,933 --> 00:37:50,477
How have you been?

377
00:37:53,605 --> 00:37:55,398
[Seokgu] Honey, what's that smell?

378
00:37:56,149 --> 00:37:58,485
Are you kidding me?
Why did you make so much?

379
00:37:58,568 --> 00:37:59,778
Looks good, doesn't it?

380
00:37:59,861 --> 00:38:02,781
You should've just made a little.
It must've been a lot of work.

381
00:38:02,864 --> 00:38:04,699
-[Hwayoung] Eat up.
-[Seokgu chuckles]

382
00:38:06,117 --> 00:38:07,786
What? Aren't you eating with me?

383
00:38:10,288 --> 00:38:11,664
I ate earlier.

384
00:38:11,748 --> 00:38:13,458
My stomach's a little upset right now.

385
00:38:13,541 --> 00:38:15,126
[Seokgu] Hey, seriously?

386
00:38:15,210 --> 00:38:16,711
Come on.

387
00:38:16,795 --> 00:38:17,879
Come sit with me.

388
00:38:17,962 --> 00:38:19,297
There we go.

389
00:38:20,006 --> 00:38:21,716
Please have a seat.

390
00:38:30,517 --> 00:38:33,895
[sighs] At least let me look at you
while I eat.

391
00:38:33,978 --> 00:38:35,146
Please.

392
00:38:37,023 --> 00:38:38,483
Thanks for the food.

393
00:38:39,275 --> 00:38:41,611
[chuckles] Looks delicious.

394
00:38:55,083 --> 00:38:56,960
-Hmm?
-[door slides]

395
00:38:58,795 --> 00:39:00,380
[Hwayoung] You must be tired.

396
00:39:00,463 --> 00:39:01,923
You can have the bed to yourself.

397
00:39:02,006 --> 00:39:03,007
Where are you going?

398
00:39:04,259 --> 00:39:05,969
I don't want to make you uncomfortable.

399
00:39:06,553 --> 00:39:08,137
We still have to be careful.

400
00:39:10,306 --> 00:39:13,268
I'm sorry, honey. Give me that.

401
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:15,728
No, you sleep here.
I'll sleep on the couch.

402
00:39:15,812 --> 00:39:17,146
Go on, get some rest.

403
00:40:50,615 --> 00:40:53,451
[Hyeongsu groans] This is ridiculous.

404
00:40:53,534 --> 00:40:56,204
That bastard should be the one moving,
not you.

405
00:40:57,497 --> 00:40:59,248
I guess this is as far as I can go.

406
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:03,419
I'm sorry for making you worry so much.

407
00:41:06,297 --> 00:41:08,383
I'll find you a lawyer at a top law firm.

408
00:41:08,925 --> 00:41:10,802
How about we take him on in a civil suit?

409
00:41:10,885 --> 00:41:13,346
That's not what we should be
talking about right now.

410
00:41:13,429 --> 00:41:14,681
[Hyeongsu] Why not?

411
00:41:14,764 --> 00:41:17,600
We shouldn't be letting that bastard
get away with it.

412
00:41:17,684 --> 00:41:18,685
[Jieun] What about her life?

413
00:41:18,768 --> 00:41:21,479
How long is she supposed to
let this case consume her?

414
00:41:23,398 --> 00:41:24,399
[Hyeongsu] But…

415
00:41:28,027 --> 00:41:29,529
Go check on the kids.

416
00:41:29,612 --> 00:41:31,990
They've been too quiet.
They might be up to something.

417
00:41:32,657 --> 00:41:35,451
Still, whatever you decide to do,

418
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:38,621
you have my full support.

419
00:41:40,456 --> 00:41:42,333
Yes. Thank you.

420
00:41:48,047 --> 00:41:49,298
[Hyeongsu] Geez.

421
00:41:59,142 --> 00:42:01,185
Are you sure you're going to be okay?

422
00:42:06,232 --> 00:42:08,985
I wanted to put everything back
the way it was.

423
00:42:13,656 --> 00:42:17,035
But like you said,
I need to take care of myself first.

424
00:42:19,203 --> 00:42:22,040
Instead of starting over
somewhere new again,

425
00:42:22,123 --> 00:42:24,375
why don't you just move in with us?

426
00:42:26,335 --> 00:42:29,297
Everywhere I go around here,
I'm reminded of what happened.

427
00:42:29,380 --> 00:42:30,882
I feel like I can't breathe.

428
00:42:36,512 --> 00:42:37,513
I feel like…

429
00:42:38,681 --> 00:42:40,933
I haven't been of much help to you.

430
00:42:41,017 --> 00:42:42,769
I'm really sorry.

431
00:42:44,896 --> 00:42:46,105
What are you talking about?

432
00:42:46,189 --> 00:42:48,566
I couldn't have made it this far
without you.

433
00:42:51,903 --> 00:42:52,945
Thanks.

434
00:42:59,327 --> 00:43:00,328
Oh, right.

435
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:02,872
Junghyeon gave me Uyeong's umbrella.

436
00:43:07,168 --> 00:43:09,796
Oh, that. You can give it to me later.

437
00:43:09,879 --> 00:43:10,880
[Jisun] Okay.

438
00:43:20,306 --> 00:43:22,183
[Seokgu, singsongy] She's here.

439
00:43:22,266 --> 00:43:24,644
Here she is.

440
00:43:24,727 --> 00:43:26,646
Look. Ta-da!

441
00:43:26,729 --> 00:43:28,606
-What's all this?
-[Seokgu chuckles]

442
00:43:28,689 --> 00:43:30,608
Look at this. Doesn't this look amazing?

443
00:43:30,691 --> 00:43:33,402
Remember how often we went
to this place for chicken feet?

444
00:43:33,486 --> 00:43:34,695
You went all the way there?

445
00:43:34,779 --> 00:43:36,405
Yeah, of course.

446
00:43:36,489 --> 00:43:38,616
The owner even remembered us.

447
00:43:38,699 --> 00:43:39,867
I told him we got married,

448
00:43:39,951 --> 00:43:42,370
and he said I must've
saved the country in a past life.

449
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:46,624
So I told him,
"I'm saving the country in this life too."

450
00:43:46,707 --> 00:43:48,584
This one won't be too spicy for you.

451
00:43:48,668 --> 00:43:50,503
It's the owner's special sauce.

452
00:43:50,586 --> 00:43:52,421
Even pregnant women and kids can enjoy it.

453
00:43:52,505 --> 00:43:54,882
Wow, looks delicious.

454
00:43:56,300 --> 00:43:57,802
Oh, man. This would be so good…

455
00:43:58,636 --> 00:43:59,887
with some soju.

456
00:44:04,183 --> 00:44:05,852
-Go ahead.
-[Seokgu exclaims]

457
00:44:11,023 --> 00:44:13,067
I noticed you'd finished
all your green juice,

458
00:44:13,151 --> 00:44:16,988
so I made you another week's worth.

459
00:44:18,906 --> 00:44:20,408
This one's yours.

460
00:44:22,410 --> 00:44:24,829
And this one's mine.

461
00:44:27,665 --> 00:44:29,542
Oh, right.

462
00:44:29,625 --> 00:44:30,877
There was one more thing.

463
00:44:30,960 --> 00:44:32,503
Is it ready?

464
00:44:32,587 --> 00:44:33,796
There we go.

465
00:44:35,381 --> 00:44:36,382
Oh, my.

466
00:44:38,467 --> 00:44:40,428
It's ready.

467
00:44:41,095 --> 00:44:43,097
THURSDAY

468
00:44:58,487 --> 00:44:59,906
Just a moment.

469
00:45:01,574 --> 00:45:02,617
[Seokgu] Huh?

470
00:45:03,201 --> 00:45:04,869
Sorry, just a moment.

471
00:45:07,747 --> 00:45:10,583
-Hey, Hwayoung.
-[door opens, closes]

472
00:45:38,402 --> 00:45:40,821
Have you decided whether to move?

473
00:45:43,407 --> 00:45:44,408
[Jisun] Yes.

474
00:45:45,576 --> 00:45:47,245
I'm going to put my place up for sale.

475
00:45:49,664 --> 00:45:50,957
But…

476
00:45:53,459 --> 00:45:56,170
I want to catch Min Junho so badly.

477
00:45:59,757 --> 00:46:02,927
Whenever I'm awake,
it's all I can think about.

478
00:46:06,347 --> 00:46:07,431
Me too.

479
00:46:14,647 --> 00:46:16,524
It's all I can think about.

480
00:46:20,236 --> 00:46:22,697
I guess the investigation
isn't going so well again.

481
00:46:30,871 --> 00:46:32,331
Is something wrong?

482
00:47:12,371 --> 00:47:14,040
[Seokgu] Is this your way of protesting?

483
00:47:18,502 --> 00:47:20,880
Because I left you alone
early in your pregnancy?

484
00:47:23,049 --> 00:47:25,426
I'm sorry I'm late.

485
00:47:26,927 --> 00:47:28,763
Something important came up, so…

486
00:47:30,306 --> 00:47:32,516
Have you eaten?

487
00:47:42,401 --> 00:47:43,444
I'm exhausted.

488
00:47:43,944 --> 00:47:45,488
I'm going to wash up and go to bed.

489
00:47:45,571 --> 00:47:46,906
[Seokgu] That's it?

490
00:47:52,036 --> 00:47:53,579
It's a confidential investigation.

491
00:47:55,498 --> 00:47:56,707
You know my job.

492
00:48:19,271 --> 00:48:20,815
Can't you just let it go?

493
00:48:23,651 --> 00:48:25,027
Why do I have to…

494
00:48:29,782 --> 00:48:32,326
You don't need to know
everything about my work.

495
00:48:33,411 --> 00:48:35,621
It's not like
you can solve my cases for me.

496
00:48:38,582 --> 00:48:40,584
Well, I need to know what it's about

497
00:48:40,668 --> 00:48:42,711
before we can decide
if I can solve it or not.

498
00:48:44,130 --> 00:48:48,050
Fine, you don't have to tell me about
your cases or investigations.

499
00:48:48,592 --> 00:48:50,845
I get that. But…

500
00:48:53,389 --> 00:48:57,852
At least tell me if you're in danger,
if you're okay,

501
00:48:58,936 --> 00:49:01,230
or if there's anything I can do to help.

502
00:49:02,523 --> 00:49:05,985
That's all I'm asking.
Don't shut your husband out like this.

503
00:49:09,071 --> 00:49:10,114
Get some rest.

504
00:49:27,548 --> 00:49:31,469
Hyunsoo, how about we play some basketball
after we eat? It's been a while.

505
00:49:33,512 --> 00:49:34,763
I have homework.

506
00:49:39,185 --> 00:49:40,186
Okay.

507
00:49:46,358 --> 00:49:47,693
Where did you go that day?

508
00:49:49,612 --> 00:49:50,613
That day?

509
00:49:51,197 --> 00:49:52,990
The day the police asked about.

510
00:49:58,078 --> 00:50:01,207
Well, I took a walk in the park

511
00:50:01,290 --> 00:50:02,917
and went for a run along the beach.

512
00:50:04,877 --> 00:50:06,045
Did you run into anyone?

513
00:50:10,299 --> 00:50:12,551
If someone saw you,
they might tell the police.

514
00:50:18,599 --> 00:50:19,642
Min Hyunsoo.

515
00:50:20,684 --> 00:50:24,605
One visit to the police station,
and now you're interrogating your own dad?

516
00:50:24,688 --> 00:50:25,689
Huh?

517
00:50:26,982 --> 00:50:28,609
Can you swear on my life?

518
00:50:33,906 --> 00:50:35,407
Of course.

519
00:50:36,075 --> 00:50:38,077
I could even swear in front of your mom.

520
00:50:42,957 --> 00:50:44,959
Just like I protected you,

521
00:50:45,543 --> 00:50:47,211
you've protected me.

522
00:50:49,380 --> 00:50:51,298
Why did you tell me to go out that day?

523
00:50:57,179 --> 00:50:58,222
That day?

524
00:51:00,099 --> 00:51:01,392
When Mom died.

525
00:51:07,064 --> 00:51:09,775
-Hyunsoo.
-You told me to go outside and play.

526
00:51:13,362 --> 00:51:15,030
But I wanted to stay with Mom.

527
00:51:20,411 --> 00:51:23,789
Your mom wasn't feeling well that day,
and you kept bothering her, so--

528
00:51:23,872 --> 00:51:26,166
-What are you talking about?

529
00:51:27,876 --> 00:51:29,962
I never bothered Mom.

530
00:51:51,191 --> 00:51:52,443
I'm sorry.

531
00:51:56,989 --> 00:51:58,991
I didn't explain to you properly

532
00:52:00,117 --> 00:52:01,744
how sick your mom was back then.

533
00:52:06,457 --> 00:52:10,419
Your mom was worried about you
right up until the end.

534
00:52:12,379 --> 00:52:14,465
Even in her final moments,

535
00:52:15,174 --> 00:52:16,884
your mom loved you

536
00:52:18,469 --> 00:52:20,095
more than anything in the world.

537
00:52:27,227 --> 00:52:28,562
I see you've been struggling.

538
00:52:30,689 --> 00:52:32,066
From now on,

539
00:52:33,609 --> 00:52:36,820
don't lie no matter what, okay?

540
00:52:38,197 --> 00:52:42,284
Not even for me or your mom.

541
00:53:06,642 --> 00:53:08,644
Hey, Lieutenant Commander Park!

542
00:53:09,478 --> 00:53:10,896
Sir! [chuckles]

543
00:53:10,979 --> 00:53:12,147
Hey, look at you.

544
00:53:12,231 --> 00:53:14,983
Looks like you've caught a lot of pirates.
You're looking good.

545
00:53:15,067 --> 00:53:17,528
Have you caught
a lot of bad guys yourself, sir?

546
00:53:17,611 --> 00:53:19,655
Why don't you come in?
You could teach my guys

547
00:53:19,738 --> 00:53:22,825
some of those fancy knife-fighting
techniques before you go.

548
00:53:22,908 --> 00:53:25,994
What, so you can put me to work
and take all the credit again?

549
00:53:26,078 --> 00:53:28,956
Hey, what credit?
I just want to show you off.

550
00:53:29,039 --> 00:53:31,792
Come on, we're both serving our country.
Would it kill you

551
00:53:31,875 --> 00:53:34,586
to make your old hometown buddy
look good in front of his men?

552
00:53:35,170 --> 00:53:37,881
When you put it that way,
I guess I should.

553
00:53:37,965 --> 00:53:39,591
-Let's go.
-No.

554
00:53:40,092 --> 00:53:41,260
They're all out right now.

555
00:53:42,136 --> 00:53:43,220
So what brings you here?

556
00:53:43,303 --> 00:53:44,847
You're here to see Inspector Lee?

557
00:53:44,930 --> 00:53:47,141
No, I came to see you, sir.

558
00:53:49,309 --> 00:53:50,519
What for?

559
00:53:52,855 --> 00:53:55,774
Looks like something big's going on
at work lately.

560
00:53:56,275 --> 00:53:59,528
Hwayoung's been acting differently,
and something just feels off.

561
00:54:01,530 --> 00:54:03,824
I mean… Why?

562
00:54:03,907 --> 00:54:06,076
Did Inspector Lee say something?

563
00:54:06,160 --> 00:54:08,203
No, it's just…

564
00:54:09,329 --> 00:54:10,914
She just seems a little different.

565
00:54:10,998 --> 00:54:13,834
It started around ten days
before I got back, I think.

566
00:54:16,795 --> 00:54:18,922
She's probably just exhausted.

567
00:54:19,006 --> 00:54:22,217
She's at that stage
where she'd be especially sensitive.

568
00:54:22,301 --> 00:54:25,888
I did notice she was working too hard,
so I told her to take some time off, but…

569
00:54:28,599 --> 00:54:33,020
Nothing happened with
a particular case or anything, did it?

570
00:54:33,103 --> 00:54:35,272
Huh? Hold on a second.

571
00:54:37,191 --> 00:54:39,318
I should get back inside.

572
00:54:40,027 --> 00:54:41,820
What did you just say? A case?

573
00:54:43,739 --> 00:54:44,823
Well, I don't know.

574
00:54:47,034 --> 00:54:49,703
You know how stressful
our job can be, right?

575
00:54:49,786 --> 00:54:52,331
Why don't you talk to her?
Tell her to take some time off?

576
00:54:52,414 --> 00:54:55,626
I should get back inside.
It was good to see you.

577
00:54:58,337 --> 00:54:59,505
Wait, sir!

578
00:55:01,423 --> 00:55:04,718
We should go for some octopus and soju
at our usual spot sometime soon.

579
00:55:04,801 --> 00:55:06,011
Of course!

580
00:55:06,094 --> 00:55:08,138
I can't today, but I'll give you a call.

581
00:55:08,889 --> 00:55:10,516
-[Seokgu] Make sure you do.
-Yeah, will do.

582
00:55:22,694 --> 00:55:23,695
[officer] Ma'am.

583
00:55:24,404 --> 00:55:26,198
I'm going to head home now.

584
00:55:26,281 --> 00:55:27,407
Yeah, sure.

585
00:55:39,920 --> 00:55:41,338
MY HUSBAND

586
00:55:41,421 --> 00:55:43,423
HAVE YOU HAD LUNCH? I'M HAVING GUKBAP

587
00:55:43,507 --> 00:55:44,925
WHAT TIME WILL YOU BE HOME?

588
00:55:59,314 --> 00:56:02,442
-[mouse clicks]
-[typing]

589
00:56:02,526 --> 00:56:06,947
LEAVE REQUEST FORM
PARK SEOKGU

590
00:56:10,576 --> 00:56:12,661
DO YOU WANT TO SAVE THIS DOCUMENT?
DON'T SAVE

591
00:56:16,415 --> 00:56:18,125
MOVE LEAVE REQUEST FORM
TO RECYCLE BIN

592
00:56:18,208 --> 00:56:19,918
MY WIFE

593
00:56:20,002 --> 00:56:21,503
[Hwayoung] <i>I'll be late again tonight.</i>

594
00:56:23,422 --> 00:56:25,507
<i>I won't be able to have dinner with you.</i>

595
00:56:26,758 --> 00:56:28,010
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

596
00:56:34,433 --> 00:56:36,435
RECYCLE BIN

597
00:56:39,313 --> 00:56:41,523
LEAVE REQUEST FORM

598
00:56:45,861 --> 00:56:49,406
NARCOTICS ANALYSIS REPORT, LEE HWAYOUNG

599
00:56:49,489 --> 00:56:51,366
RESTORE

600
00:57:01,001 --> 00:57:04,671
4. RESULTS OF ANALYSIS
GAMMA-HYDROXYBUTYRIC ACID, GHB

601
00:57:04,755 --> 00:57:06,131
POSITIVE

602
00:57:18,352 --> 00:57:20,103
You post your personal information here,

603
00:57:20,187 --> 00:57:23,732
change your profile picture,
and wait for a response.

604
00:57:23,815 --> 00:57:26,610
Once you're verified,
they send you the dark web address.

605
00:57:28,445 --> 00:57:30,322
Apparently, the address, the prices,

606
00:57:30,405 --> 00:57:33,116
and even the delivery methods
change all the time.

607
00:57:36,161 --> 00:57:39,706
So this is how
Mr. Park Junghyeon bought GHB?

608
00:57:42,000 --> 00:57:44,586
If we actually catch the people
distributing it this way,

609
00:57:45,212 --> 00:57:47,047
do you think we'll get a list of buyers?

610
00:57:47,923 --> 00:57:49,591
Even if there is one,

611
00:57:49,675 --> 00:57:51,802
there's no guarantee
Min Junho will be on it.

612
00:57:51,885 --> 00:57:52,886
It's a start.

613
00:57:53,887 --> 00:57:56,264
Given the nature of this area,

614
00:57:56,348 --> 00:57:59,434
there's a good chance
both the sellers and buyers live nearby.

615
00:58:00,018 --> 00:58:03,355
Please, let us get lucky on the first try.

616
00:58:03,438 --> 00:58:06,066
We just need to find something,
even the smallest lead,

617
00:58:06,149 --> 00:58:08,485
so that we can apply for a search warrant.

618
00:58:09,403 --> 00:58:10,862
I'll do whatever I can to help.

619
00:58:12,155 --> 00:58:14,366
But nothing dangerous like last time.

620
00:58:14,908 --> 00:58:20,080
Don't ever forget you promised me
you'd never provoke Min Junho again.

621
00:59:03,999 --> 00:59:05,542
Does your husband know?

622
00:59:19,389 --> 00:59:23,852
I thought I'd tell him
once the case was solved, but…

623
00:59:26,021 --> 00:59:27,564
I don't think I can.

624
00:59:30,442 --> 00:59:32,319
I can't bear the thought of watching him…

625
00:59:34,654 --> 00:59:36,031
get his heart broken.

626
00:59:36,114 --> 00:59:37,491
I had no idea Min Junho

627
00:59:38,909 --> 00:59:42,204
was crazy enough
to sexually assault a police officer.

628
00:59:42,287 --> 00:59:43,622
He was mocking me.

629
00:59:46,333 --> 00:59:48,960
Because he's so sure
he'll never get caught.

630
00:59:54,549 --> 00:59:55,675
Stay here.

631
01:00:08,396 --> 01:00:09,773
[Jisun] <i>What was that?</i>

632
01:00:09,856 --> 01:00:11,024
<i>Are we okay?</i>

633
01:00:11,107 --> 01:00:12,567
[Hwayoung] <i>I guess it was nothing.</i>

634
01:00:15,320 --> 01:00:16,488
<i>I'll take you home.</i>

635
01:00:16,988 --> 01:00:18,740
[Jisun] <i>It's okay.</i>

636
01:00:19,491 --> 01:00:21,368
[Hwayoung] <i>It's dangerous,</i>
<i>and it's getting late.</i>

637
01:00:22,577 --> 01:00:23,703
[Jisun] <i>Thank you.</i>

638
01:01:06,413 --> 01:01:07,539
[Junho] Hello.

639
01:01:09,583 --> 01:01:11,751
[nurse] Dr. Min, have you heard?

640
01:01:11,835 --> 01:01:12,878
Heard what?

641
01:01:14,170 --> 01:01:15,422
[nurse] You haven't heard.

642
01:01:16,882 --> 01:01:18,258
You know, Yunji.

643
01:01:18,758 --> 01:01:19,968
She was in intensive care

644
01:01:20,051 --> 01:01:22,429
because she wasn't
recovering well after surgery.

645
01:01:22,512 --> 01:01:23,513
Yes.

646
01:01:25,724 --> 01:01:28,476
She passed away last night.

647
01:01:35,901 --> 01:01:37,652
You know what everyone's saying?

648
01:01:38,320 --> 01:01:41,072
That she'd still be alive
if you'd operated on her back then.

649
01:01:41,573 --> 01:01:44,117
All because that woman went around
spreading false rumors.

650
01:01:45,535 --> 01:01:47,537
She didn't just make your life miserable.

651
01:01:47,621 --> 01:01:49,164
She's a murderer.

652
01:01:49,247 --> 01:01:50,248
That's…

653
01:01:51,249 --> 01:01:52,667
going a bit too far.

654
01:01:54,961 --> 01:01:56,504
Please be mindful of how you speak.

655
01:01:58,381 --> 01:01:59,382
Okay.

656
01:02:41,716 --> 01:02:43,718
Sir, you can go in now.

657
01:03:32,142 --> 01:03:36,062
THE PERFECT LIE

658
01:04:00,170 --> 01:04:03,506
How do you manage to sleep at night?

659
01:04:04,966 --> 01:04:08,636
As you know, there are things
we'd never want them to know.

660
01:04:09,262 --> 01:04:10,847
<i>If she doesn't turn herself in,</i>

661
01:04:12,098 --> 01:04:13,975
things will only get worse.

662
01:04:14,726 --> 01:04:17,062
I can't even trust
the people I used to trust.

663
01:04:17,145 --> 01:04:18,396
[Junho] <i>I'm giving you a chance.</i>

664
01:04:18,480 --> 01:04:20,940
It's the only way to protect your sister.

665
01:04:21,983 --> 01:04:25,195
[Jieun] You want me to have
my own sister committed?

666
01:04:25,278 --> 01:04:28,448
[Jisun] <i>You were the only person</i>
<i>in the world I could trust.</i>

667
01:04:28,531 --> 01:04:30,867
<i>So how could you lie to me, Jieun?</i>

668
01:04:46,132 --> 01:04:47,717
THE PERFECT LIE

669
01:04:47,801 --> 01:04:49,803
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi
